record Page<T>(IReadOnlyList<T> Items, int PageNumber, int TotalPages, bool HasNext);

fund-csharp/07-generics-and-constraints/.explanation:
Validate first, then compute the page count with ceiling division and slice with Skip/Take:

```csharp
var totalPages = (items.Count + size - 1) / size;
var slice = items.Skip((page - 1) * size).Take(size).ToList();
return new Page<T>(slice, page, totalPages, page < totalPages);
```

`ToList()` materialises the page, so the result does not re-run the query (topic 09). The method never mentions a concrete element type, which is why the same code serves ints and strings.

